#!/usr/bin/env nu

# Activity Duration Processor
# Automatically calculates and inserts durations for any activity time range entries
# Processes entries like "s:: 0025-0755" -> "s:: 7hr 30min 0025-0755"
# Works with any activity code (single or multi-letter): w::, e::, m::, test::, etc.
# Supports shorthand: "p:: 0845-55" -> "p:: 10min 0845-0855"
# Created: 2025-09-07, Expanded: 2025-09-09
#
# Modes:
#   activity-duration-processor PATH   — read/write file on disk
#   activity-duration-processor -      — stdin → stdout (Helix :pipe, no :reload race)
#   activity-duration-processor        — process recently modified vault .md files
#
# Spoken keys (Handy / STT): "key sleep" → sleep::  before durations run.
# Trigger is the word "key" plus a phrase in spoken-key-table, plus
# hyphen/dot stems from Social/*.md (person and couple keys).
# Lines without \bkey\s skip the spoken-key table (keeps Space+P catch-up cheap).
# Spoken clocks: "o one twenty to o seven ten" → 0120-0710, then duration.
# Spoken quantities: "seven thousand steps" → 7000-steps; "forty-five minutes" → 45min.
# Lint: glue units; default-quantity-rules (walk → steps, sauna → min).
# State: "key state tired 8" / "tired eight" → state:: tired-8
# Helix: Space+p current line; Space+P whole buffer.
# Do not put key:: literals in Handy custom_words.

def regex-escape-spoken [s: string] {
    $s | str replace --all --regex '([.\\+*?()|\[\]{}^$])' '\$1'
}

